.TH ZLINE 1 "September 2026" "zline 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zline \- fast, modern, and flexible pure-Zsh prompt engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zline
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B zline preset
\fIPRESET\fR [\fIFLAGS\fR...]
.br
.B zline style
\fISTYLE\fR [\fIFLAGS\fR...]
.br
.B zline init
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBzline\fR is an ultra-fast, modern, and flexible pure-Zsh prompt engine designed as a streamlined replacement for Powerlevel10k.
It delivers sub-millisecond synchronous rendering (< 0.7 ms) with zero subprocess forks on the critical prompt path,
relying exclusively on native Zsh parameter expansions, built-in modules, and an event-driven architecture.
.PP
Heavy background operations (such as full Git working tree status) are computed asynchronously
via non-blocking pipes and ZLE file descriptor handlers (\fBzle -F\fR), ensuring the interactive shell
never stutters or drops user keystrokes.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration in \fBzline\fR is declarative and concise, avoiding the need for hundreds of global environment variables.
Prompts are defined using standard Zsh arrays:
.RS
.nf
# Set visual preset
zline preset powerline --transient

# Define left prompt segments
zline_left=(
  'dir --shorten 1 --alias github.com=gith --anchor git'
  'git --clean 2 --dirty 3'
  newline
  prompt_char
)

# Define right prompt segments
zline_right=(
  'status --hide-zero'
  'exec_time --min 2'
)

# Initialize prompt engine
zline init
.fi
.RE

.SH PRESETS
\fBzline\fR includes four built-in presets:
.TP
.B powerline
Classic multi-colored background blocks joined by Powerline arrow glyphs (U+E0B0, U+E0B2).
.TP
.B lean
Modern, flat, space-separated layout with crisp foreground colors.
.TP
.B rainbow
High-contrast, vivid powerline blocks designed for rapid visual parsing.
.TP
.B pure
Minimalist two-line prompt inspired by Sindre Sorhus's Pure prompt.

.SH BUILT-IN SEGMENTS
.TP
.B dir
Displays current working directory.
.RS
.IP "\fB--shorten\fR \fIN\fR"
Shortens intermediate directory components to \fIN\fR characters (e.g. \fB--shorten 1\fR produces \fB~/s/g/c/zline\fR).
.IP "\fB--keep-last\fR \fIN\fR"
Number of trailing directory components to keep full (default: 1).
.IP "\fB--alias\fR \fIpattern=replacement\fR"
Substitutes matching path components (e.g. \fB--alias github.com=gith\fR).
.IP "\fB--anchor\fR \fIgit\fR"
Anchors at Git repository root, shortening paths above the repository but keeping the repository name full.
.IP "\fB--format\fR \fIfunc_name\fR"
Delegates path formatting to a custom Zsh function setting \fB$REPLY\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B git
Fast Git status segment.
.RS
.IP "\fB--clean\fR \fIcolor\fR"
Color used when working tree is clean (default: 2 / green).
.IP "\fB--dirty\fR \fIcolor\fR"
Color used when working tree has changes (default: 3 / yellow).
.IP "\fB--ahead\fR \fIcolor\fR"
Color used when branch is ahead of remote (default: 12 / bright-blue).
.RE
.TP
.B status
Command exit status indicator.
.RS
.IP "\fB--hide-zero\fR"
Hides status badge when command succeeded (exit code 0).
.IP "\fB--show-zero\fR"
Displays 0 in green when command succeeded.
.RE
.TP
.B exec_time
Execution duration for previous command.
.RS
.IP "\fB--min\fR \fIN\fR"
Minimum duration in seconds before displaying execution time (default: 2).
.RE
.TP
.B prompt_char
Active prompt symbol.
.RS
.IP "\fB--symbol\fR \fIsym\fR"
Character to display (default: ❯).
.IP "\fB--root\fR \fIsym\fR"
Character to display for root user (default: #).
.IP "\fB--error\fR \fIcolor\fR"
Color to display when previous command failed (default: 9 / bright-red).
.RE
.TP
.B venv
Python virtualenv, Conda, or Poetry active environment.
.TP
.B node
Active Node.js version from \fI.node-version\fR, \fI.nvmrc\fR, or \fB$NODE_VERSION\fR.
.TP
.B k8s
Active Kubernetes context extracted from \fB$KUBECONFIG\fR or \fI~/.kube/config\fR.
.TP
.B time
Formatted current timestamp without subprocess forks.
.TP
.B jobs
Count of running background jobs from \fB$jobstates\fR.
.TP
.B aws
Active AWS profile and region.
.TP
.B rust
Active Rust toolchain or version from \fIrust-toolchain\fR or \fICargo.toml\fR.
.TP
.B golang
Active Go version from \fIgo.mod\fR.
.TP
.B terraform
Active Terraform workspace from \fB$TF_WORKSPACE\fR or \fI.terraform/environment\fR.
.TP
.B docker
Active Docker context from \fB$DOCKER_CONTEXT\fR or \fI~/.docker/config.json\fR.
.TP
.B package
Project version from \fIpackage.json\fR or \fICargo.toml\fR.
.TP
.B user_host
Displays username and hostname in SSH sessions or when root.
.TP
.B battery
Battery charge percentage and charging status.
.TP
.B ruby
Active Ruby version from \fI.ruby-version\fR or \fIGemfile\fR.
.TP
.B php
Active PHP version from \fI.php-version\fR or \fIcomposer.json\fR.
.TP
.B java
Active Java version from \fI.java-version\fR, \fIpom.xml\fR, or \fIbuild.gradle\fR.
.TP
.B dotnet
Active .NET version from \fIglobal.json\fR or project files.

.SH COLOR PALETTE
\fBzline\fR standardizes on Base16 / Term16 colors (0\(en15) to guarantee seamless harmony with any terminal color scheme:
.IP "0 / 8"
black / bright-black (grey)
.IP "1 / 9"
red / bright-red (errors, root)
.IP "2 / 10"
green / bright-green (clean git, success)
.IP "3 / 11"
yellow / bright-yellow (dirty git, warnings)
.IP "4 / 12"
blue / bright-blue (directory, branch)
.IP "5 / 13"
magenta / bright-magenta (language runtimes)
.IP "6 / 14"
cyan / bright-cyan (cloud environments)
.IP "7 / 15"
white / bright-white (primary prompt symbol)

.SH MODERN TERMINAL PROTOCOLS
\fBzline\fR natively integrates modern terminal standards:
.TP
.B OSC 133
Semantic shell integration markings (prompt start, command start, command output, return code) for Ghostty, Kitty, WezTerm, iTerm2, and VS Code.
.TP
.B OSC 7
Current working directory reporting for automatic directory inheritance across tabs and splits.
.TP
.B OSC 8
Terminal hyperlinks for clickable file paths and Git repositories.

.SH CLI COMMANDS
.TP
\fBzline preset\fR \fIname\fR [\fIoptions...\fR]
Loads a preset theme configuration.
.TP
\fBzline style\fR \fIname\fR [\fIoptions...\fR]
Configures visual styling (\fB--transient\fR, \fB--ascii\fR, \fB--no-osc\fR).
.TP
\fBzline init\fR
Compiles segments and initializes hooks.
.TP
\fBzline bench\fR [\fIiterations\fR]
Runs execution latency benchmark over \fIiterations\fR (default: 1000).
.TP
\fBzline version\fR
Prints active version.
.TP
\fBzline doctor\fR
Runs comprehensive health and environment diagnostics.
.TP
\fBzline configure\fR [\fIoptions...\fR]
Interactive setup wizard and config generator.
.TP
\fBzline compile\fR
Pre-compiles scripts to memory-mapped Zsh wordcode (.zwc).
.TP
\fBzline clean\fR
Removes compiled .zwc wordcode files.
.TP
\fBzline migrate\fR [\fIp10k_file\fR] [\fIoutput_file\fR]
Automatically translates Powerlevel10k configuration to zline.

